The bug was caused by the presence of external pull-up resistors on the PMIC_IRQB and PMIC_KEYINB lines, which required the pull control to be disabled in the device tree configuration. The previous configuration did not account for these external resistors, leading to improper handling of interrupts from the MAX8997, thus preventing the correct operation of the RTC alarm wakeup feature.

